_3D.calculateMUDimensions [SimTalk]
Calculates the dimensions of the MU designated by <Path> from its graphic.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>._3D.calculateMUDimensions([OnlyVisibleGroups:boolean:=false])
Parameter
The optional parameter OnlyVisibleGroups of data type boolean sets if the dimensions of all graphic
groups are to be computed (false) or only of the visible graphic groups (true).
After Plant Simulation has executed the method, the Length, Width, and Height of the MU match the
dimensions of the graphic. Plant Simulation uses the zero point of the graphic to calculate the booking
point.
Default Value of the Parameter
The default value is false.
Example
.MUs.Part._3D.calculateMUDimensions(true)
See also
Calculate Dimensions from 3D
_3D.calculateMUDimensions [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-1193
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

_3D.exchangeGraphic [SimTalk]
Exchanges the entire graphic of the selected object designated by <Path> with the graphic you imported
from a file.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>._3D.exchangeGraphic(FilePath:string[, 
UseNewGraphicMeasurement:boolean:=false]) → boolean
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter FilePath of data type string sets the path and the name of the file you want to import.
• The optional parameter UseNewGraphicMeasurement of data type boolean sets if the new graphic
measurements are also to be used for the simulation measurements of the MU.
If you specify true and the object is a MU and if the attribute _3D.ScaleAutomatically of the
loaded .s3d file is set to false, this attribute is set to true again and the graphic measurements are
applied to the simulation. In all other cases the method does not execute anything in addition.
Default Value of the Parameter
The default value is false.
Return Value
The return value has the data type boolean.
Example
MyFrame._3D.exchangeGraphic("C:\Program Files\Siemens\Plant Simulation 
2606\3D\s3D-graphics\Lathe.s3d")
See also
Exchange Graphics
_3D.ScaleAutomatically [SimTalk]
_3D.exchangeGraphic [SimTalk]
12-1194 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

_3D.ExcludeFromShowContentOfLocation [SimTalk]
Hides (true) or shows (false) the object designated by <Path> from the outside representation of the
object. Also hides Connectors that are connected with hidden objects.
Remarks
After assigning true, the outside representation of the selected object is only visible within its location,
and not in the location of its location. This makes, for example, sense for the EventController, for Methods,
for DataTables, etc., which are needed to define and control the simulation but not to illustrate the
simulated scene.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>._3D.ExcludeFromShowContentOfLocation:boolean
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type boolean.
Example
Station._3D.ExcludeFromShowContentOfLocation := true
See also
Edit 3D Properties [dialog] > Graphics [tab] > Exclude From "Show content" of the Location
_3D.ExcludeFromShowContentOfLocation [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-1195
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

_3D.exportAsJt [SimTalk]
Exports the designated graphic or the designated 3D object of the object designated by <Path> as a .JT file.
Remarks
_3D.exportAsJt exports only graphics which are part of the object.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>._3D.exportAsJt(FilePath:string[, OptimizeForCAD:boolean := false, 
ExcludeInvisibleParts:boolean := false]) → boolean
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter FilePath of data type string sets the path to the target file.
• The optional parameter OptimizeForCAD of data type boolean sets if the structure of the graphic will be
optimized for CAD applications such as NX (true) or for other applications such as Plant Simulation or
Teamcenter Visualization (false).
Default Value of the Parameter
The default value is false.
• The optional parameter ExcludeInvisibleParts of data type boolean sets if all graphics of the object
(false or not set) are going to be exported or if only those graphics that would be visible if you would
open the object in a window (true)
Default Value of the Parameter
The default value is false.
When you export a graphic as a Jt file and when you activate Optimize for CAD, captions and logical
object are excluded.
Logical objects are:
• EventController
• FlowControl
• Cycle
_3D.exportAsJt [SimTalk]
12-1196 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• Exporter
• Broker
• ShiftCalendar
• LockoutZone
• All InformationFlow objects
• All UserInterface objects
• All GA objects
Return Value
The return value has the data type boolean.
true if the file could be exported with graphics.
false if nothing was left to be exported.
Example
.MaterialFlow.Frame.exportAsJt("D:\MyS3D\MyFrame.jt")
See also
_3D.exportModelingViewBitmap [SimTalk]
_3D.exportPlanningViewBitmap [SimTalk]
