_3D.exportModelingViewBitmap [SimTalk]
Exports the 3D modeling view scene of the object designated by <Path> as a .PNG file.
Remarks
The parameters CameraPosition and CameraRotation correspond to the parameters CameraPosition and
CameraPosition of the function F3DconfigureView. If you create SimTalk code with F3DconfigureView, you
can also use it with slight modifications here.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>._3D.exportModelingViewBitmap(FilePath:string, Width:integer, 
Height:integer[, CameraPosition:length[3], CameraRotationX:real, 
CameraRotationZ:real]) → boolean
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter FilePath of data type string sets the path to the target file.
• The parameter Width of data type integer sets the width in pixels in the target file.
• The parameter Height of data type integer sets the height in pixels in the target file.
• The optional parameter CameraPosition is an array of data type length with three values. It sets the
camera position in the scene.
• The optional parameter CameraRotationX of data type real sets the rotation angle of the camera around
the x-axis.
• The optional parameter CameraRotationZ of data type real sets the rotation angle of the camera around
the z-axis.
Note
You can either specify all three camera parameters or none of them. If you do not specify them, Plant
Simulation creates a bitmap of the entire scene.
_3D.exportModelingViewBitmap [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-1199
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Return Value
The return value has the data type boolean.
true if Plant Simulation was able to create the bitmap.
Example
.Models.Model._3D.exportModelingViewBitmap("D:\FactoryLibraries\MyFrame", 
100, 100, [2,3,2], 2,2)
See also
_3D.exportAsJt [SimTalk]
_3D.exportAsS3D [SimTalk]
F3DconfigureView [SimTalk]
