_3D.exportPlanningViewBitmap [SimTalk]
Exports the 3D planning view scene of the object designated by <Path> as a .PNG file.
Remarks
The parameters ViewPosition and Zoom correspond to the parameters ViewPosition and Zoom of the
function F3DconfigurePlanningView. If you create SimTalk code with F3DconfigurePlanningView, you can
also use it with slight modifications here.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>._3D.exportPlanningViewBitmap(FilePath:string, Width:integer, 
Height:integer[, ViewPosition:length[2], Zoom:real]) → boolean
_3D.exportPlanningViewBitmap [SimTalk]
12-1200 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter FilePath of data type string sets the path to the target file.
• The parameter Width of data type integer sets the width in pixels in the target file.
• The parameter Height of data type integer sets the height in pixels in the target file.
• The optional parameter ViewPosition is an array of data type length with two values. It sets the view
position in the scene.
• The optional parameter Zoom of data type real sets the zoom factor in the view.
Note
You can only specify both the view position and the zoom factor together. If you do not specify them,
Plant Simulation creates a bitmap of the entire scene.
Return Value
The return value has the data type boolean.
true if Plant Simulation was able to create the bitmap.
Example
.Models.Model._3D.exportPlanningViewBitmap("D:\FactoryLibraries\MyFrame", 
100, 100, [2,3], 3)
