_3D.optimizeObject [SimTalk]
Optimizes the 3D object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
The object can either be a simulation object or an animatable object.
Note
As you cannot restore discarded data, we advise to optimize the structure of the object after you are
done modeling the object. Optimizing the 3D graphic improves performance.
We also recommend to save the model under a different name before optimizing it. This way you can
return to the state the model had before optimizing it in case the optimized model reports errors or does
not meet your expectations.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>_3D.optimizeObject(WithContainedObjects:boolean, 
OptimizeInheritance:boolean, OptimizeGraphicStructure:boolean)
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter WithContainedObjects of data type boolean sets if, starting from the object
designated by <Path>, the entire partial structure will be optimized, for example the entire
model for basis._3D.optimizeObject or the entire folder named MaterialFlow for the
instruction .MaterialFlow._3D.optimizeObject (true). Specify false to only optimize the
object itself.
• The parameter OptimizeInheritance of data type boolean sets if setting Optimize 3D Attribute
Inheritance will be activated and if Plant Simulation attempts to (true):
◦ Activate inheritance of 3D attributes whose values uniquely match the corresponding value of its
origin. Graphics inheritance is never activated.
◦ Replace MU Animation Paths for individual matrix places, with names such as #0#0, etc., with an
Animation Area if this change is possible without a position change of the animation.
• The parameter OptimizeGraphicStructure of data type boolean sets if the setting Optimize 3D Graphic
Structure will be activated and if Plant Simulation applies the optimization setting Flatten structure,
without the setting Keep Grouping to all editable graphics (true).
_3D.optimizeObject [SimTalk]
12-1206 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

If this parameter is true, Plant Simulation optimizes the model with activated setting Preserve
References. This is intended to prevent that the model size increases after optimizing the model. In
some cases it might prevent an optimal optimization result for the graphic structure.
Example
.Models.Model._3D.optimizeObject(true, true, false)
See also
Step 2: Flatten Structure
Preserve References
Optimize Model
Optimize Selected Graphic
Optimizing a Graphic
Optimizing the Model
_3D.optimizeObject [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-1207
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

_3D.ShowContent [SimTalk]
Shows (true) or hides (false) the outside representation of the objects that are contained within the
object designated by <Path> in 3D windows that show the designated object from the outside.
Remarks
The outside representation of an object consists of its visible external graphic groups and, for Frames only,
the outside representation of its contained objects for which _3D.ExcludeFromShowContentOfLocation is
set to false.
Contained objects, for which 3D.ExcludeFromShowContentOfLocation is set to true, never are visible
outward, independent of the setting in the outside representation of this object.
_3D.ShowContent only applies for objects, which can contain MUs and for the Frame. Objects, which can
contain MUs, are most of the material flow objects, plus Container and Transporter and their animatable
objects.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>._3D.ShowContent:boolean
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type boolean.
Example
Station._3D.ShowContent := true
See also
Edit 3D Properties [dialog] > Graphics [tab] > Show Content
_3D.ExcludeFromShowContentOfLocation [SimTalk]
_3D.ShowContent [SimTalk]
