Detailed Access To Graphics
_Detailed Access To Graphics
SimTalk provides the attributes and methods listed in the table of contents to the left for accessing the
object graphics.
Detailed Access To Graphics
Plant Simulation Help 12-1209
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

addGraphicTransformation [SimTalk]
Adds an additional transformation to an existing transformation of the designated graphic of the object
designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Assigning the method deactivates graphic inheritance.
You cannot assign the method if the graphic is an automatically generated graphic group or if the graphic
is located in an automatically generated graphic group.
Let’s suppose that a graphic is translated by the coordinates (3, 0, 0) from its origin and its basic
orientation, and rotated by 30° around its y-axis.
Applying the method addGraphicTransformation to this graphic with a translation of (2, 0, 0) and a
uniform scaling factor of 2 results in a graphic translation which first translates it by the coordinates (3, 0,
0), then rotates it by 30° around the y-axis, then translates it by (2, 0, 0), and finally scales the resulting
translation by a factor of 2 in all directions. Note the sequence is important. It is, for example, not possible
to combine the translations into one.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.addGraphicTransformation(Position:length[3], RotationAngle:real, 
RotationAxis:real[3], Scale:real/real[3])
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter Position is an array of data type length with three values. They designate the position of
the graphic.
• The parameter RotationAngle of data type real sets its rotation angle.
• The parameter RotationAxis is an array of data type real with three values. They designate the rotation
axis of the graphic.
• The parameter Scale sets the scale of the graphic.
You can either specify a single parameter of data type real, which sets a uniform scaling.
Or you can specify an array of data type real with three values. They designate the scaling factors along
the X-axis, the Y-axis, and the Z-axis.
addGraphicTransformation [SimTalk]
12-1210 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Examples
MyStation.getGraphic("default", [1,4]).addGraphicTransformation([3,2,1], 
30, [0,0,-1], 2)
MyStation.getGraphic("deco", [1,4]).addGraphicTransformation([3,2,1], 30, 
[0,0,-1], 2)
See also
Transformation
_3D.getGraphic [SimTalk]
addGraphicTransformation [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-1211
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

