InternalGraphicType [SimTalk]
Returns the type of the graphic or graphic group designated by <Path>.
Type
Read-only attribute
Syntax
<Path>.InternalGraphicType → string
Return Value
The return value has the data type string.
Plant Simulation returns one of the following types:
Composite graphics
• FactoryWalls are Factory Walls. After optimizing a parent graphic this graphic might possibly not be
recognized as factory walls but as a Shape or a GroupNode.
• Fence is a Fence. After optimizing a parent graphic this graphic might possibly not be recognized as a
fence but as a GroupNode.
• GraphicGroup is a graphic group. This is the case for all graphics whose access arose with an empty
array in the second parameter of _3D.getGraphic or if you only specified a single parameter.
• GroupNode is a normal group node that is formed by groupGraphics for example.
• Instance is a special group node which can only contain a single child graphic.
• Rack is a Rack. After optimizing a parent graphic this graphic might possibly not be recognized as a rack
but as a Shape or a GroupNode.
• Stairs is a Staircase. After optimizing a parent graphic this graphic might possibly not be recognized as
a set of stairs but as a Shape or a GroupNode.
• Switch is a special group node that always shows one if its children only.
Simple graphics
• BarredArea is a Barred Area. After optimizing a parent graphic this graphic might possibly not be
recognized as a barred area but as a Shape.
• Box is a Box. After optimizing a parent graphic this graphic might possibly not be recognized as a box
but as a Shape.
InternalGraphicType [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-1217
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• Dimensionings are Measurements within your model. After optimizing a parent graphic this graphic
might possibly not be recognized as dimensionings but as a Shape.
• Shape is a graphic that is not subdivided any more, which contains its graphics data itself, as opposed to
GroupNode.
Example
var graphic := MyStation._3D.getGraphic("default", [1])
if graphic.InternalGraphicType = "Fence"
   graphic.restoreCutouts
end
See also
_3D.getGraphic [SimTalk]
InternalGraphicType [SimTalk]
12-1218 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

makeAnimatableObject [SimTalk]
Creates an animatable object for the object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
makeAnimatableObject takes the designated graphic, extracts it from the original object, and uses this
graphic for the animatable object to be created.
If the graphic, from which the animatable object is created, is not part of the default graphics group, the
method creates a graphics group with the name of the graphics group where the graphic to be extracted
is located. In previous versions Plant Simulation created the graphics group within the default graphics
group.
Assigning the method deactivates graphic inheritance.
You cannot assign the method if the graphic is an automatically generated graphic group or if the graphic
is located in an automatically generated graphic group.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.makeAnimatableObject(ObjectName:string, 
ExtractAtBoundingBoxBase:boolean[, ExtractionOffset:length[3], 
SwapXAndZAxis:boolean]) → any
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter ObjectName of data type string sets the name of the animatable object.
• The parameter ExtractAtBoundingBoxBase of data type real sets if the insertion position of the new
object is determined based on the bounding box of the graphic (true) or not (false).
• The optional parameter ExtractionOffset is an array of data type length with three values which sets the
offset of the insertion position. If you do not specify the value, the method uses the values [0,0,0].
• The optional parameter SwapXAndZAxis of data type boolean sets if the graphics of the animatable
object will be rotated by 90° around the y-axis, thus swapping the x-axis and the z-axis, while looking
the same from the outside (true). If you do not specify the value, the method uses the value false.
makeAnimatableObject [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-1219
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Return Value
The return value of data type any designates the newly created animatable object.
Examples
var tool := MyStation._3D.getGraphic("default", 
["tool"]).makeAnimatableObject("toolHead",true, [0,0,0]) 
tool.JointType := "Revolute Joint"
MyStation._3D.getGraphic("default", 
["tool"]).makeAnimatableObject("toolHead",true, [0,0,0]) 
MyStation._3D.getObject("toolHead").JointType := "Revolute Joint" 
// This line of code accomplishes the same as the second line of code in 
the first example.
See also
Make Animatable Object
delete [SimTalk] - animatable object
