MaterialTransparency [SimTalk]
Sets the transparency of the material of the graphic designated by <Path>.
Remarks
When assigning a value to the attribute, we automatically set the material to active
(MaterialActive := true).
You can only access the attribute if the material is active.
Assigning the attribute deactivates graphic inheritance.
You cannot assign the attribute when the graphic is an automatically generated graphic group or when the
graphic is located in an automatically generated graphic group.
Note
If your model contains several partially or fully transparent graphics behind each other from your current
view point, it can happen that some or all of these graphics look wrong or seem to be missing.
This is due to heuristics without which the rendering performance would drastically decrease.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.MaterialTransparency:real
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type real between 0 and 1.
Example
MyStation._3D.getGraphic("default", [3,3]).MaterialTransparency := 0.9
See also
Edit 3D Properties [dialog] > Material [tab] > Transparency [material]
