ObstacleForWorker [SimTalk]
Sets the settings for the obstacle for the Worker of the graphic designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Assigning the attribute deactivates graphic inheritance.
You cannot assign the attribute when the graphic is an automatically generated graphic group or when the
graphic is located in an automatically generated graphic group.
Note
The attribute is not available for those objects, which you cannot insert directly into a Frame, for
example MUs or folders. Graphics of type BarredArea do not provide the attribute either.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.ObstacleForWorker:string
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type string.
You can enter one of the following settings for graphics of type Stairs:
Bounding Box Graphics Sides
ObstacleForWorker [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-1235
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Bounding Box Graphics Sides
• "(None)"
The staircase is no obstacle for the Worker who can walk through it.
• "Bounding box"
The bounding box of the staircase is an obstacle for the Worker around which he has to walk.
• "Sides"
This setting computes the obstacle for the Worker in a way that:
◦ An accessible entrance toward which the staircase lead or an exit from which the staircase leads away
is not obscured by the obstacle.
◦ The obstacle is limited to the applicable range for the respective simulation-relevant height.
You can specify one of these settings for the graphics types FactoryWalls, Fence, GroupNode, Instance,
Mezzanine, Rack, and Switch, compare InternalGraphicType:
• "(None)"
The graphic is no obstacle for the Worker who can walk through it or across it.
• "Bounding box"
The bounding box of the graphic is an obstacle for the Worker around which he has to walk.
• "Graphics"
The graphics of the graphics are an obstacle for the Worker around which he has to walk.
You can specify one of these settings for graphics of type Box and Shape:
• "(None)"
The box is no obstacle for the Worker who can walk through it or across it.
• "Bounding box"
The bounding box of the box is an obstacle for the Worker around which he has to walk.
ObstacleForWorker [SimTalk]
12-1236 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Example
Station._3D.ObstacleForWorker := "Graphics"
Station._3D.getGraphic("default", [2]).ObstacleForWorker := "(None)"
See also
Worker Width [model settings]/Worker Width [preferences]
Edit 3D Properties [dialog] > Graphics [tab] > Obstacle for the Worker [drop-down list]
