optimizeByPruningTinyGraphics [SimTalk]
Optimizes the graphic designated by <Path> by pruning its tiny graphics, i.e., it removes all component
graphics which individually fit within the cube designated by the parameter BoundingCubeSideLength.
Remarks
Assigning the method deactivates graphic inheritance.
You cannot assign the method if the graphic is an automatically generated graphic group or if the graphic
is located in an automatically generated graphic group.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.optimizeByPruningTinyGraphics(BoundingCubeSideLength:length)
Parameter
The parameter BoundingCubeSizeLength is an array with a single value of data type real. It designates the
size of the bounding box.
Example
.Models.Model._3D.getGraphic("deco",[1]).optimizeByPruningTinyGraphics([1], 
0.001)
See also
Optimize Selected Graphic
Step 1: Prune Tiny Graphics
_3D.getGraphic [SimTalk]
optimizeByPruningTinyGraphics [SimTalk]
