Rotation [SimTalk] - graphic
Sets the rotation of the designated graphic designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Assigning the attribute deactivates graphic inheritance.
You cannot assign the attribute when the graphic is an automatically generated graphic group or when the
graphic is located in an automatically generated graphic group.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.Rotation:real/real[4]
Assignment Value
You can specify:
• A value of data type real which sets the rotation around the negative Z-axis at the position at which you
inserted the object.
• An array of data type real with four values. The first value designates the angle, the remaining three
values designate the components of the rotation axis at the position at which you inserted the object.
Return Value
The return value is an array of data type real with four values.
Examples
var a : any := MyStation._3D.getGraphic("default", [1]).Rotation 
// returns an array of size 4
MyStation._3D.getGraphic("default", [1]).Rotation := 30 
// rotates the graphic by 30 degrees
MyStation._3D.getGraphic("default", [1]).Rotation := [45, 0, 1, 0] 
// rotates the graphic by 45 degrees around the Y-axis
